# Flashing: at most three flashes in any one second (WCAG 2.2 success criterion 2.3.1, general flash)
law flash-three-per-second
kind audit
claim the luminance series is sampled 60 times a second, so a window of 60 samples is one second
claim a flash is a pair of opposing luminance changes of at least 0.1 (10% of the maximum) where the darker end is below 0.8
claim the series is the mean luminance of the reference frame, a measure of the whole frame and not of a 25% area of the visual field
source https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#three-flashes-or-below-threshold

x-input luminance list of number
x-metric samples = count(luminance)
x-series excess = flashes_above(luminance, 60, 0.1, 0.8, 3)

begin audit
audit flash-three-per-second
evidence samples
expect excess == 0
end audit

verdict the verdict of the audit block for the given measurements
